{"abstract":[{"text":"The key used to look up an entry in a strings file or strings dictionary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"file.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/localizedstringkey"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LocalizedStringKey","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Initializers for several SwiftUI types – such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Toggle"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Picker"},{"type":"text","text":" and others –  implicitly look up a localized string when you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provide a string literal. When you use the initializer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text(\"Hello\")"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI creates a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for you and uses that to look up a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"localization of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hello"},{"type":"text","text":" string. This works because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conforms to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/ExpressibleByStringLiteral"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Types whose initializers take a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" usually have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a corresponding initializer that accepts a parameter that conforms to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/StringProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":". Passing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" variable to these initializers avoids localization, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"usually appropriate when the variable contains a user-provided value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As a general rule, use a string literal argument when you want","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"localization, and a string variable argument when you don’t. In the case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where you want to localize the value of a string variable, use the string to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"create a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedStringKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example shows how to create "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text"},{"type":"text","text":" instances both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with and without localization. The title parameter provided to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Section"},{"type":"text","text":" is a literal string, so SwiftUI creates a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocalizedStringKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for it. However, the string entries in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageStore.today"},{"type":"text","text":" array are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" variables, so the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text"},{"type":"text","text":" views"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the list use the string values verbatim."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["List {","    Section(header: Text(\"Today\")) {","        ForEach(messageStore.today) { message in","            Text(message.title)","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the app is localized into Japanese with the following"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"translation of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.strings"},{"type":"text","text":" file:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"other","code":["\"Today\" = \"今日\";"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When run in Japanese, the example produces a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list like the following, localizing “Today” for the section header, but not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the list items.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"LocalizedStringKey","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI18LocalizedStringKeyV","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LocalizedStringKey"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LocalizedStringKey"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LocalizedStringKey","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SQ","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s43ExpressibleByExtendedGra